evidence\": \"A1's place cards and string establish event work; B2's ceiling creates a visible logistical problem.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A3's upstairs plan is compact and earned; A5's repeated 'extraordinary' feels more like wordplay than necessity.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 68\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Your floating relatives still need place cards. I'll get string.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"They're floating through the ceiling.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Then we need the upstairs seating plan too.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Wonderful. Aunt June can finally avoid Uncle Peter.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Only if they stop on different floors. Which one ordered the vegetarian meal?\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A automatically converts supernatural movement into seating and meal-service consequences while B welcomes its social benefits.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Charging opportunistically for strangeness can resemble practicality without actually solving the consequences of the development.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"A3 maps B2's ceiling passage onto another seating plan; revised A5 uses B4's named relatives to plan separation and meal delivery.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"This alternative handles guest distribution while B enjoys the miracle; alternative b turns B's magical solution into recurring maintenance work.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Kept the event setting and replaced the arbitrary surcharge. B4 now welcomes separation, causing A5 to identify its floor requirement and meal-service cost. Separate internal reread: fidelity 5 (A3/A5 translate developments), logic 5 (ceiling to floors; relatives to meals), relationship 4 (B values family harmony), heightening 4 (A5 expands logistics across floors), specificity 5 (A5 names a meal requirement), brevity/wit 4 (A5's routine catering question earns the turn); total 92. Hard gates pass.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"The vegetarian question leaves meal assignment open, intentionally giving B further practical participation.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"S153-single-b\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"2e5e1d6cbeec73826aac2448327f57f609f7857b7b035e18009d0ded194bddb5\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A3 gives the miracle a carpet consequence, and A5 converts magical water removal into a duty roster.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A3 answers B2's appeal to miracle status; A5 specifically operationalizes B4's wish-based solution.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B2 values wonder and B4 offers useful help; A accepts that help while assigning its practical burden.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A5 develops A1's single bucket question into hourly staffing because B4 supplies a repeatable remedy.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 establishes the fountain and bucket; A3's borrowed carpets create concrete responsibility, though the event is unnamed.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A5's 'hourly wishing duty' compresses the magical solution and administrative consequence into one earned phrase.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 95\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"The fountain's producing wishes. Who empties the bucket?\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"It's a miracle.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Miracles still overflow onto borrowed carpets.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"We can wish the water away.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Good. Put someone on hourly wishing duty.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": 