ence\": \"A3 adopts B2's 'poetic' qualification; A5 uses B4's 'Nobody' wording more than its practical obstacle.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"B2 clarifies poetic intent and B4 states impossibility, but neither changes the available means of fulfillment.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 2, \"evidence\": \"A5 rebukes the original promise without increasing its present obligation beyond A3's breakfast deadline.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1's prepared shelf and A3's breakfast deadline make the impossible delivery concrete.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A3's poetic delivery is character-driven; A5's 'consulted nobody' is chiefly a wordplay finish.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 69\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"You promised me a sunrise in a box last anniversary. The shelf's still ready.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"That was poetic. I can bring you breakfast in bed.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Lovely. Put the box beside the tray when it's ready.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"It won't be ready this anniversary either.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Then I'll leave the shelf clear another year. Please don't buy anything that needs that space.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A keeps an old impossible gift promise active by treating substitute offers and further delay as delivery arrangements rather than cancellation.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Literal-mindedness could misunderstand poetry once; this card sustains the obligation across elapsed time and acknowledged delay.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"Revised A1 names the previous anniversary and A5 reserves the shelf for another year after B4 explicitly postpones fulfillment.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Alternative a uses patient domestic accommodation; alternative b turns a future guest's delay into continuing dinner preparation.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Kept the boxed sunrise and shelf, adding anniversary history and B's affectionate substitute. B2's breakfast becomes a delivery surface; B4's delay produces another year's reserved space. Separate internal reread: fidelity 5 (A1/A5 maintain the old obligation), logic 5 (A3 uses tray; A5 uses annual delay), relationship 4 (B offers care), heightening 4 (A5 reserves household space for a year), specificity 5 (anniversary and shelf connect), brevity/wit 4 (A5's shopping restriction follows patience); total 92. Hard gates pass.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"The comic pressure is quiet and patient; actors should avoid turning A's reservation of space into a sarcastic punishment.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"S156-single-b\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"bd3936ba6fa87d4122e740d41f8d4aec90210ce469909f2da494c30406015b27\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 prepares for a promised future guest and A3 insists on the date, but A5 personifies the promise instead of maintaining a concrete obligation.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A3 answers B2's delay; A5's demand that 'the promise' explain itself is weakly connected to B4's time-travel objection.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"B2 and B4 resist the timing, but provide little beyond repeated inability.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 2, \"evidence\": \"A5 replaces the awaited person with an abstract promise without developing the plate or dinner commitment.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A1 establishes a plate and next-century guest; A5 makes the playable addressee of the demand unclear.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A3's 'Saturday, not eventually' is concise; A5's abstract personification weakens the finish.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 63\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"I've set a plate for that guest from next century you promised last Christmas.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"They can't arrive for another hundred years. We should eat.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Go ahead. I'll keep their dinner warm.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"The oven won't last a hundred years.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Then the replacement needs a warming drawer. Your guest is still expected.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A treats the impossible guest's century-long delay as an outstanding hosting obligation requiring continued preparation.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Practical adaptation to time travel alone would not require the old promise to remain the source of responsibility.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"Revised A1 identifies last Christmas's promise, and A5 explicitly keeps B's guest expected while planning replacement equipment.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Alternative b gives the continuing obligation an appliance consequence; alternative a expresses patient commitment through reserved domestic space.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Preserved the future guest and plate while supplying promise history and a concrete delay. B2 prompts meal preservation; B4's oven lifespan prompts the replacement requirement. Separate internal reread: fidelity 5 (A1/A5 keep the promise active), logic 5 (A3 uses mealtime; A5 uses oven failure), relationship 4 (B wants to eat and challenges feasibility), heightening 4 (A5 extends preparation into replacement purchasing), specificity 5 (plate, dinner and warming drawer connect), brevity/wit 4 (A5 applies ordinary shopping to extraordinary delay); total 92. Hard gates pass.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"The imagined hundred-year appliance succession