lity 5 (A1/A3 establish the prior self), logic 4 (A3/A5 explain each anomaly through wrong familiar causes), relationship 4 (B wants tea), heightening 4 (A5 proceeds toward servicing), specificity 5 (manual, cup and plug support play), brevity/wit 4 (A5's routine procedure sustains certainty); total 88. Hard gates pass.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"The bracket diagnosis is deliberately wrong for a kettle; its plausibility comes from A's obsolete certainty, not sound repair advice.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"S158-single-b\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"fb4207fcf968413bc7aded8e1c7b5848e8e82f44d3dad604d3091aedd1595a0b\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 contrasts old doors with Thursdays and A5 invokes old handles, though A's former identity is only implied.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3 turns B2's Thursday into a fitting error and A5 answers B4's passage question with the handle.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"B4 wants to get through, but B2 simply repeats A1's impossibility without adding pressure.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A5 repeats ordinary hardware certainty without showing how Thursday changes the repair or consequence.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1's door into Thursday is immediately imaginable and A5 gives a concrete handle.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3's incorrectly fitted calendar is economical; A5's old handles sustains the voice but adds little.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 74\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"When I was caretaker, this door opened into the staffroom. What's all this Thursday business?\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"It opens into next Thursday. My coat's still in there.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Calendar's been fitted backwards. I'll turn it round.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Now it's last Thursday. My coat hasn't arrived yet.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Wrong-size calendar. Fetch the old one. We never lost a coat to a properly fitted door.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A inhabits a former caretaker's certainty and reduces temporal impossibilities to familiar installation faults.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Nostalgic complaint would mourn the old world without actively explaining each new impossibility through its assumptions.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"Revised A1 names the old caretaker role, A3 diagnoses reversed fitting, and A5 diagnoses size after B4 changes the temporal result.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"This alternative lets an attempted ordinary fix worsen B's coat problem; alternative a shifts diagnoses while B's floating kettle actually supplies tea.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Added caretaker history, a missing coat and a consequential attempted fix. B2 causes calendar reversal; B4's resulting last Thursday causes a size diagnosis and request for old equipment. Separate internal reread: fidelity 5 (A1/A5 perform former authority), logic 5 (A3 attempts reversal; A5 responds to changed date), relationship 4 (B needs a coat), heightening 4 (A5 doubles down after failure), specificity 5 (staffroom and coat anchor time travel), brevity/wit 4 (A5's fitting maxim expresses old certainty); total 92. Hard gates pass.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"B4 supplies the result of A3's proposed adjustment; the spoken exchange leaves any physical enactment optional.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"S159-single-a\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"e47b78bb2f9a8824de6ef50726ca94a475234c7e3c212d3781c5c0b628e24224\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A1 fears reality hearing the claim, while A3 and A5 urgently replace impossible descriptions with ordinary ones.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A3 normalizes B2's floating report; A5 specifically recasts B4's ceiling height as excellent posture.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B2 insists on the visible fact and B4 reports its worsening, forcing A to keep finding protective language.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A5 must normalize a ceiling-bound chair, making A3's normal-height explanation untenable.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 supplies a floating chair and B4 gives it a clear ceiling destination, though the wider setting is sparse.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A5's 'Excellent posture' is a compact furniture-specific euphemism caused directly by B4.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 92\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Don't call Mum's floating chair impossible. Reality might hear. Pass her the potatoes.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"She's above the table. I can't reach.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Just a high chair. Fetch the stepladder; dinner's getting cold.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"She's at the ceiling now. I'm calling for help.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Call it room service. Ask for a taller ladder and three desserts upstairs. We're having a perfectly ordinary family dinner.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A urgently disguises an acknowledged impossibility in ordinary language to prevent reality from noticing the doubt.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Denying evidence from stubborn certainty lacks the fear of attracting attention that motivates A's verbal concealment.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"A1 names reality as a possible listener; revised A3 disguises Mu